From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:21:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] origin-work snapshot: use WAL so a save never locks
 out the remote-links cold read

kanban-ec72354e6b (hermes-hub, 2026-11-14 03:06/05:04/09:01 UTC): the remote-links background rebuild
failed with 'database is locked' at kanban_lockguard._apply PRAGMA journal_mode while opening
~/.hermes/origin-work.db for its cold-start snapshot read, and was dropped ('background rebuild failed;
serving the previous projection'). The same file logged 27 'origin-work snapshot not saved: database is
locked' in errors.log. origin-work.db was the one kanban store still in the rollback journal
(PRAGMA journal_mode -> delete, 23 MB, multi-MB row per scope rewritten by every process), so a
commit's EXCLUSIVE lock refused every reader for longer than the 0.5 s open budget, and any reader's
SHARED lock failed the writers.

The save path now upgrades the file through apply_wal_with_fallback (keeps its WAL-reset-bug gate,
network/cross-VM fallbacks and never-live-downgrade invariant), bounds the -wal file and re-applies
the OFD lock guard, like kanban_db_connect does for boards.

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_origin_snapshot_wal.py fails 3/4 on the base (cold read raises
'database is locked' at kanban_lockguard.py:140 while another connection holds BEGIN EXCLUSIVE; save
raises under an open reader; existing delete-mode file stays delete) and passes 5/5 with the fix;
mutants (drop guard / journal_size_limit / WAL condition / WAL upgrade) are all killed. 42 kanban
activity/origin/remote/lockguard/generation files: 772 passed.
